      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "The number of subscribers to a video channel is given by $S(t)=5\\cdot (2.4)^{t},$ where $t$ is the time in days since the channel was opened. How many subscribers will the channel have after a week? Round your answer to the nearest integer.",
      "worked_solution": "To get the number of subscribers to the video channel after a week ($7$ days), we evaluate the function at $t=7.$ Substituting $t=7$ into the function $S(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(7) & =5\\cdot (2.4)^{7} \\\\  & ≈2\\,293.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, after a week, the video channel will have $2\\,293$ subscribers.",
